"""A seeded corpus of sealed-run records, generated by code, each labelled with its true verdict.

`Record` writes a record root as `docs/sealed-runs.md` (layer 5) lays it out: manifest, role dirs with
role.json, transcripts, proxy.jsonl, guard.jsonl and an end.json whose hashes `hash_role_files` computes.
`CASES` lists named cases, each with the verdict the run truly deserves (`expected`) and, for a void one, the
reason kind that should be among its reasons. `known_miss` marks the hard cases the audit gets wrong on
purpose-built grounds (see their notes); `ops/seal_audit_rates.py` measures them, and a test fails if one of
them starts being called correctly so the label gets revisited.

Cases are written from what the real tools print (`fatal: unable to access ...`, a hook denial with
`is_error` true), not from what the audit looks for.
"""

